# Force a textual diff for source and script files (#827).
#
# git decides binary-vs-text by looking for a NUL byte in the blob, and the pre-#825
# memory-drain.mjs delimited its op_id hash fields with literal NULs. The result: `git diff`
# reported a JavaScript source file as *binary* and showed no diff for it — through a review,
# a merge, and a public push. An invisible byte silently removed a file from review.
#
# The NULs there are gone, but this keeps the class from recurring for any source file: git
# renders a textual diff no matter what lands inside it, so an accidental NUL becomes a visible
# control character in the diff instead of a silent "Bin N -> M bytes, 0 insertions(+), 0
# deletions(-)". scripts/check-nul-bytes.sh (CI: the shellcheck job) is the other half — it
# fails the build outright if one ever lands, rather than relying on a reviewer to notice.
#
# Originally *.mjs only; widened to every source extension actually tracked in this repo
# (re-derived from `git ls-files | sed -E 's/.*\.//' | sort -u`, not remembered — keep the two
# lists, here and in check-nul-bytes.sh's EXTENSIONS, in sync by hand). Binary asset extensions
# (images, lockfiles, compiled artifacts) are deliberately excluded: they legitimately contain
# arbitrary bytes and forcing a textual diff on them would be noise, not safety.
*.go    diff text
*.js    diff text
*.mjs   diff text
*.ts    diff text
*.py    diff text
*.php   diff text
*.sh    diff text
*.yml   diff text
*.yaml  diff text
*.json  diff text
*.proto diff text
*.kt    diff text
*.kts   diff text
*.swift diff text
*.css   diff text
*.html  diff text
*.toml  diff text
*.md    diff text
